{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1525223-nemeses-and-adversaries-organizational-horrors-brainstorming","id":1525223,"title":"Nemeses and Adversaries [Organizational Horrors- Brainstorming]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-08T15:57:09-08:00","id":1525223,"title":"Nemeses and Adversaries [Organizational Horrors- Brainstorming]","content":"So one of the things I thought about while doing my AKD splat book long time ago was making a subsection of Night Horrors dedicated for that specific organization. While I played around with other concepts from that book (Sovereignty, Paragons, Chapters, Conspiracy-based Undertaking, Cabals, etc), this one was more or less was just left floating around, so I thought it might be a time to return and revisit that idea and see how it applies to all orgs.<br /> <br /> The basic idea behind those Horrors is that while every org has their own personal enemies, we could adapt those enemies into being a bit more &quot;personal&quot;, tying them to the themes and philosophies that the conspiracies themselves express. While we could do it with singular Horrors or NPCs, I generally always preferred them taking the form of &quot;species&quot; or cultural groups, but that's just my personal preference. As such, I'm doing some brainstorming along those lines, so please let me know what do you think! First post will be about the Core Eight conspiracies, but hopefully I will discuss other orgs as we move along through them- Currently I plan on 4 such adversaries per Conspiracy and 2 per compact, but we'll see how things roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Aegis Kai Doru:</b> this one is more or less set, as I've wrote down the whole goddamn fan supplement for them in the first place, so basically I need to choose which Night Horrors are the most &quot;in theme&quot; for them. While I tried to make them all appropriate to a degree, there are some which I find as more interesting and connected to the AKD: the first are the <b>Adonai Aretz</b>, which are a &quot;Hunter name&quot; for the Baal Haddad, with the common twist of them not necessary being werebulls but using all kinds of livestock animals (but I am willing to maintain the Bull-only angle as it is very fitting to the AKD). The main reason I find them as appropriate is the combination of shapeshifters + bulls + the use of relics in the form of idols are all just a perfect fit for a AKD antagonist. The second are the <b>Daktyloi</b> (a revision of my Cabiri)- it is expected that a Arisen-like entity would serve as an antagonist to the conspiracy, and the twist of the Daktyloi being Lifeless mummies who are powered by relics due to a flawed attempt at recreating the Rite of Return makes them into basically living relics, which would again put them at odds with the conspiracy. In order to close the Witches angle, I originally gave them mechanics for the Bound under the name of the <b>Gigantes</b>, making them into mythical monstrosities trapped in their own labyrinth like worlds, which could bestow great power on those who are faithful to them, but I guess that if it doesn't scratch the itch something along the lines of the <b>Hem Khet</b>, the relic devourers, could work. Finally, the fourth spot I keep for the Agathodaimon, who serve as metaphysical agents of the Labyrinths built by the conspiracy, created through geomantic resonances and relic occult energies, turning them into angel-like beings.<br /> <br /> <b>Ascending Ones:</b> while the AO do not have any specialized enemies to the same degree as the AKD, they do have certain enemies with which they hold special connection. Vampires are obviously the first, through their connection to the Cult of Set. A form of vampiric blood alchemists sounds like the best fit for them, or potentially a form of alchemical blood demon that the followers of Set craft using their own blood sorcery? Could even be called the <b>Typhoon Beast</b>. Another possibility would be using <b>Sekhmet</b> as a model, with those horrors being regular people who fall under sudden vampiric frenzy which transforms them into monsters- but we could also just use the <b>Brain Eating Ants</b> as a vampiric entity related to the time of witchcraft as described in the Empty Pharaoh section. The other connection is Promethean, which would give us a nice way to tie the <b>Djinn</b> as a variant form of Qashmalim, adding some twist to their behavior such as them being bound to certain vessels, and potentially their ability to grant wishes or something along those lines. Mortal Remains adds Mummies as another enemies which the conspiracy had to deal with through the ages, and while using some kind of demon from Egyptian mythology could be cool, I thought about using something a bit.. different. The AO are a ancient conspiracy with presence all across the world- a Amkhat like monster produced through the poison-alchemy ritual of <b>Gu</b> sounds like something that could be interesting to explore through this project. Alternatively, the Gu might be a product of blood magic, while the Mummy niche will be filled by the sorcerous creation of the Ants. Finally, I think that the last adversary should be <b>Prophets</b>- the conspiracy looks after them, after all, seeking to recruit them to the conspiracy. Who knows what kinds of terrifying miracles they might work as they invoke the name of God?<br /> <br /> <b>Cheiron:</b> Cheiron have a few things which we may need to tackle to deal with them. First would be the Beast angle, specifically with Cheiron being the teacher of Heracles, them weaving different monster parts together as a parody of Kinship and how their Slasher section basically describe Heroes before they were a thing. All of this leads me to think about a Horror called <b>Centaurs</b>, who are amalgamations weaved completely from the dead flesh of monsters which are created to hunt down other monsters, as they are able to collect their organs and add them to theirs, and also are able to perform thaumatechnology on people without the fancy equipment of the conspiracy in order to &quot;heal&quot; them. The second Horror is probably filled by a Deviant related monster- either some sort of a deviant or a monster created to hunt them down. Maybe we could style it as <b>Hemitheoi</b>, the demigods which the conspiracy creates through its experiments with &quot;ambrosia&quot;. After all, Cheiron was the one who made heroes, it makes sense that the conspiracy will do the same. As for the third Horror I consider a Contagion based one- Witch Finders already mentions how Cheiron might be connected to a Pandora Box like object which spreads a flesh mutating plague, which is an option- let's call them the <b>Anesidora</b>, the Gift Givers, walking natural hazards who bear a special form of the Contagion. Finally, as Cheiron seems to imply some strange, eldritch entities, we might have them in the form of the <b>Cabeiri</b>, who serve as alien entities which seem to reach from far worlds, and who might be related to the origin of the Board of Directors.<br /> <br /> <b>Council of Bones:</b> the CoB seems to have two main points of focus- the dead and slashers. In terms of a slasher, we could potentially have a twist here and combine them with the Eaters of the Dead, having a slasher who kills ghosts- the <b>Shrouded</b> could be their temporary name, as they reap apart ghosts and wear their ectoplasm as clothes. The dead themselves could be a wide enough wealth of possibilities- for example, we could start with a zombie variant called <b>Wights</b>, which we could base around a earlier micro template I wrote called Jackals- those are people which Death forgot to &quot;collect&quot;, leaving them dead but moving and with a burning need to eat flesh to maintain their humanity. A incorporeal form of undead could be given as <b>Wraiths</b>, ghosts which have somehow managed to capture a soul, making them much more &quot;human&quot; yet at the cost of becoming unstable and dangerous. Finally I think that another ephemeral threat would be the <b>Shells</b>, entities composed from amalgamated memories which were exchanged so much that they incarnate themselves within the dead ectoplasm and create horrifying melds of shadows.<br /> <br /> <b>Lucifuge:</b> demons, demons, and a bit more demons. I think that at the very least, an actual writeup for <b>Infernals</b> and the Possessed they create is required for the Lucifuge. Beyond that, we could use the <b>Furies</b> as a special form of demonic beings that hunt down evil and other demons, putting them in a strange position for the Lucifuge as the demons themselves are evil beyond any reasonable doubt, yet they &quot;use&quot; it for &quot;good&quot; acts. I also think that a God-Machine like demons are also of interest- perhaps a specific form of Angels called the <b>Archons</b>, the Grand Builders who enslave civilizations in order to form and protect Infrastructures and which seem to decay when exposed to Infernal beings- finding a way to differentiate them from regular angels is required, but I think that we could do so by focusing around building as a theme- instead of needs an Infrastructure to exist, they are entities which create and power the occult matrix, and are devoted to protect them from corruption. While I considered some form of Fiends for the last entry, I think that what truly scares the Lucifuge even more than demons are (actual) angels- so let's put here the <b>Elohim</b>, beings of raw, divine power who are incarnated from the hypothetical Empyrean with a single goal- to burn out all evil, and no, redemption is not an option. (Having some Abyssal horror might also be cool. God, I may end up extending this project to 5 Horrors per conspiracy and 2 for Compacts).<br /> <br /> <b>Malleus Maleficarum:</b> yeah, this one is pretty easy to follow. First, vampires- let's have a form of &quot;holy vampirism&quot;- heck, let's just go with <b>Daywalkers</b> (I considered the Blood Angels from the Testament of Longinus, but they were already covered in RfR 2e). Let's have vampires who have found &quot;redeemed&quot; themselves, becoming mad horrors which will no longer burn, and let's give them some sort of &quot;divine revelations&quot; and the ability to work miracles. That's basically the MM's worst nightmare. Next- witches. Again, let's go with the standard biblical horror and let's have <b>warlocks</b>, people who have gained supernatural capabilities by selling their soul to Satan. Yes, let's just be simple- Soulless witches who are obsessed with Vice, we don't need something more complex than that. As for demons... that's where it becomes a bit more tricky. I think that we could play on all the different sources of Benedictions (Theban Sorcery, God Machine, Sekhem Sorcery) to fill this point and make some sort of specialized Fiends- let's call them <b>Scourges</b>. Those demons are powered by guilt, possessing those who have committed crimes yet refuse to confess for their actions, constantly punishing them and feasting on their misery. Finally, I think that something that could fit the God Machine is appropriate- let's call it <b>Saints</b>, spirits of people who died as sacrifices in the name of their values, becoming divine in death and being bound into a strange, celestial Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> <b>Task Force: Valkyrie:</b> this one is a bit more complicated to consider but let's see what we have. Let's start from the easy part- Nazi Vampires. Those will be vampires who have a special ability called &quot;blood refinement&quot;, which basically allows them to create special ghouls called <b>Ubermensch</b>- people who basically had their blood replaced with Vitae granting them tremendous power yet they are fully dependent on vampires to replenish their blood once their Vitae burns out. For the second one, I think about a deviant-like horror- the <b>Flygja</b>. Some sort of an AI helpers that inhabits android forms to help with the Vigil- but sometimes might also hack the RFID chip to take over a warm, welcoming body and &quot;helping&quot; the hunter directly (think the AI from Project Freelancer in Red vs Blue). Next, let's just have <b>Valkyries</b>, like the ones I wrote for my Awful Ice project. The Chooser of the Slain, who show up when strange Auroras burn in the sky, collecting dead hunters who fell in their Vigil to fight the coming &quot;war&quot;. Finally, let's have something truly weird with the <b>Code: Yggdrasil</b>- a strange algorithm where pieces of it are found in strange computers all around the world, causing strange (specifically interdimensional) phenomena to occur while the hunters to TFV are tasked with finding the processes which run them and collect them back to base for unknown purposes.<br /> <br /> <b>VASCU:</b> slashers, psychics, deviants let's go. In terms of slashers, let's start from the basics of having a type of slashers that, for some reason, does not obey the regular rules- perhaps one that &quot;hacks&quot; the psychic processing abilities of the Wintergreen Process, or perhaps a slasher produced by the same methodology. The result is <b>Faded</b>, slashers that leave a psychic shadow whenever they kill which consumes evidence and corrupts Clues, making them invisible for both forensics and empathic senses. Moving to psychics, let's have the <b>Psychopomps</b>- they are seers blessed with the ability to see coming death, making them invaluable when hunting down slashers, yet using their deathsight has the price of establishing a empathic connection with the cause of death, which draws the slashers to them. Now, for deviants, let's have a fun little Deviant conspiracy for VASCU to deal with- the <b>Black Sun</b>, a strange group of elites that offers those they deem as &quot;worthy&quot; as sacrifices to alien gods, and sometimes those entities instead bless the conspiracy with the Flayed- their own personal Deviants. Finally, VASCU had been blamed for God Machine involvement for a while, so let's also play with it- the <b>Umbrals</b>, strange angelic beings who commune through mirrors and reflections which try to commune with VASCU agents by wearing their own faces and offering strange insight in exchange for bargains. <br /> <br /> Well, that's what I currently have for the main conspiracies. Please let me know what do you think, while I try to brainstorm some Compact based Horrors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T09:32:08-08:00","id":1525255,"title":"","content":"So I translated the post into an outline including all future sections. As you can see it is a huge project, so if any of you wish to contribute in some manner please let me know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19VwQJg7aUn5mzLp47i5Ul_OQC3xw8sp1KHXtRF9BTXE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19VwQJg7aUn5mzLp47i5Ul_OQC3xw8sp1KHXtRF9BTXE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19VwQJg7aUn5mzLp47i5Ul_OQC3xw8sp1KHXtRF9BTXE/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/19VwQJg7aUn5mzLp47i5Ul_OQC3xw8sp1KHXtRF9BTXE/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T12:51:41-08:00","id":1525266,"title":"","content":"So this is why you've been silent from the compact Vigil ascendants. What a great reason! Oh and are the faded not considered a slasher undertaking? Or does this mean for your headcanon VASCU has two slasher undertakings (faded and the Noise)<br /> <br /> I have some suggestions, but do you want the compact enemies to also be, at most, splat adjacent to corebook monsters? Like how AO seems to have Kindred, but they are blood alchemy practicing kindred?<br /> <br /> For the crossroad convoy, I think pandorans would actually make sense, or something related to prometheans. Leaning into them as walking wastelands and wanderers (prometheans) or as strange road sightings that seem to move (pandorans). Another possible horror could be something related to roads themselves rather than an individual horror type. Perhaps a vehicle related horror?<br /> <br /> EDIT: the Valkries are an interesting piece for TFV. They seem to be the only supernatural not based on some occult science/technology. I do wonder how they relate to TFV","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 11-09-2023, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T15:18:31-08:00","id":1525273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1525223-nemeses-and-adversaries-organizational-horrors-brainstorming?p=1525266#post1525266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this is why you've been silent from the compact Vigil ascendants. What a great reason! Oh and are the faded not considered a slasher undertaking? Or does this mean for your headcanon VASCU has two slasher undertakings (faded and the Noise)</div> </div> </div> </div>Two points- first, the Noise are specifically fallen VASCU hunters, the Faded might be so but aren't really a product of the conspiracy as much as its antithesis. The second is that the Faded aren't actually an Undertaking- they are meant to be an additional effect that slashers with psychic abilities develop. Some are not slashers yet- but this is a benefit which lingers towards slasherhood. Fun for everyone, I know.<br /> <br /> (note to myself, make some Undertaking pitches for the TtF orgs)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have some suggestions, but do you want the compact enemies to also be, at most, splat adjacent to corebook monsters? Like how AO seems to have Kindred, but they are blood alchemy practicing kindred? </div> </div> </div>Those monsters don't need to be splat adjacent, it is just a helpful tool as many orgs do have a preferred enemy along those lines. So as long as it fits the themes of the org, I'm open for all suggestions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the crossroad convoy, I think pandorans would actually make sense, or something related to prometheans. Leaning into them as walking wastelands and wanderers (prometheans) or as strange road sightings that seem to move (pandorans). Another possible horror could be something related to roads themselves rather than an individual horror type. Perhaps a vehicle related horror? </div> </div> </div>Something along the lines of Promethean does sound fitting from the reasons you noted. Probably would require some twist to make them more than &quot;just pandorans&quot;, I think. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: the Valkries are an interesting piece for TFV. They seem to be the only supernatural not based on some occult science/technology. I do wonder how they relate to TFV </div> </div> </div>As mentioned, the Valkyries (or the Dissir) have a writeup for my Awful Ice project (it is in my homewbrew sig, under Promethean). Let's say that in relation to the TFV, the conspiracy itself isn't sure how they are connected to them, but TFV have some occult (even if not supernatural) undertones, and as those hunters <i>don't</i> use supernatural powers in their Vigil, it could be that the Chooser of the Slain would deem their warriors as more fitting for Ragnarok- and when they need soldiers, they are not above making some new slain to choose from.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T20:20:45-08:00","id":1525284,"title":"","content":"Union- have you ever read The Outsider by Stephen King? The union could have a horror like that. One that impersonates beloved (and genuinely good) pillars of a community in order to make them appear rephrensible so the community turns on them. You could go the other way around and have a horror that ingratiates itself as pillar of the community, but in reality is doing so to subvert it to its own ends. But that latter could just be vampires. Perhaps instead, a special kind of Tainted place. Something invoking the old stereotype of the &quot;bad&quot; part of town everyone avoids.<br /> <br /> Ashwood abbey: honestly, something drug related may be good. I think they could use some demon, infernal or not, as a horror. We already have warlocks and furies and scourges, so what about Tempters? I know that's another name overlapping with a splat but still. There may be some worth in taking such an icon and having it be thematically subverted from a creature that you are slowly seduced by into sin into one eagerly sought out, perhaps to the point it's very role becomes unique to the Abbey. I think one horror you could benefit from making is one that REALLY leans into the &quot;it's not human, so what's it matter&quot; angle. Finally, perhaps one that ruins the ability to be entertained through vice (or capital Vice)? Whether a phenomenon or horror, it may be interesting to have something that causes ennui through indulging in the excesses an Abbey member usually does, which would threaten the very reason they even do any of the things they do (not that it's justified in the first place, but perspective)<br /> <br /> Network 0: def a digital virus. <br /> <br /> Division 6: Rebel Agents. Those agents who have Awakened, but whose training with the division has made a new kind of Banisher that is unable to get rid of their shard of the abyss. The result is a &quot;rebel&quot; who has it out for the Division while still able to completely suppress magic. For some strange reason may be wanted alive by Mr. Jones. Another option could be some special type of abyssal verge that represent what happens when reality doesn't just reach its breaking point but is utterly shattered.<br /> <br /> Keepers of the Source: let them talk to mother earth my guy. Its spirit HAS to exist. No way only the other planets get them<br /> <br /> MM: Short aside for this conspiracy. Perhaps these &quot;Saints&quot; could hold the key to methods to avoid the wrath of God? Like maybe the MM has VERY mimicked knowledge of modern day plagues that may come forth, and seek to stop/avoid them? Like with slaughtering lamb and putting blood above the doors of houses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T11:45:31-08:00","id":1525319,"title":"","content":"I wanted to ask about your stance on Inferno Demons. Compacts and Conspiracies that specialize in them (Malleus Maleficarum, The Lucifuge, The Long Night) do so through Christian lens. If we assume that these demons work as described in the Inferno supplement - creating their own backstories out of whole cloth, could they create one that is so &quot;out there&quot; that established exorcists would be at loss? With contemporary proliferation of popular fiction, an Acathartoi could swipe their backstory from a cartoon, Lovecraft fanfic, or a collectible card game wiki. Is that idea usable to you?<br /> <br /> Also, I think Loyalists of Thule should get Nazis. Not Zombie Nazis, or wizard Nazis. Just Nazis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T14:03:08-08:00","id":1525325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1525223-nemeses-and-adversaries-organizational-horrors-brainstorming?p=1525284#post1525284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Union- have you ever read The Outsider by Stephen King? The union could have a horror like that. One that impersonates beloved (and genuinely good) pillars of a community in order to make them appear rephrensible so the community turns on them. You could go the other way around and have a horror that ingratiates itself as pillar of the community, but in reality is doing so to subvert it to its own ends. But that latter could just be vampires. Perhaps instead, a special kind of Tainted place. Something invoking the old stereotype of the &quot;bad&quot; part of town everyone avoids.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read The Outsider, but I did already had similar idea in relation to WandaVision. Some sort of a memory interloper that creates a &quot;community&quot; around it/shapes it to act in a certain manner. I assume that both ideas derive from the same themes, so I'll have to check it out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ashwood abbey: honestly, something drug related may be good. I think they could use some demon, infernal or not, as a horror. We already have warlocks and furies and scourges, so what about Tempters? I know that's another name overlapping with a splat but still. There may be some worth in taking such an icon and having it be thematically subverted from a creature that you are slowly seduced by into sin into one eagerly sought out, perhaps to the point it's very role becomes unique to the Abbey. I think one horror you could benefit from making is one that REALLY leans into the &quot;it's not human, so what's it matter&quot; angle. Finally, perhaps one that ruins the ability to be entertained through vice (or capital Vice)? Whether a phenomenon or horror, it may be interesting to have something that causes ennui through indulging in the excesses an Abbey member usually does, which would threaten the very reason they even do any of the things they do (not that it's justified in the first place, but perspective) </div> </div> </div>Tempters are indeed something I considered, alongside Maenads due to the whole Bacchanal thing they have going on. The other options also sound like an interesting concept to develop (potentially the Tempters could be connected to the ennui thing- they consume the Willpower you should have gotten from fulfilling your Vice, causing you to doing it more and more just top get the rush. Basically an analogy to drug addiction- it makes you feel good, but you need more of it as you become addicted)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Division 6: Rebel Agents. Those agents who have Awakened, but whose training with the division has made a new kind of Banisher that is unable to get rid of their shard of the abyss. The result is a &quot;rebel&quot; who has it out for the Division while still able to completely suppress magic. For some strange reason may be wanted alive by Mr. Jones. Another option could be some special type of abyssal verge that represent what happens when reality doesn't just reach its breaking point but is utterly shattered. </div> </div> </div>Interesting concept. Abyssal horrors of some kind is probably a must for them, in some shape or form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Keepers of the Source: let them talk to mother earth my guy. Its spirit HAS to exist. No way only the other planets get them </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that this book is exactly the place to deal with CofD's theological question of &quot;Where the F is Gaea?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> MM: Short aside for this conspiracy. Perhaps these &quot;Saints&quot; could hold the key to methods to avoid the wrath of God? Like maybe the MM has VERY mimicked knowledge of modern day plagues that may come forth, and seek to stop/avoid them? Like with slaughtering lamb and putting blood above the doors of houses? </div> </div> </div>Ahmm I'm still considering how to exactly write down the &quot;Saints&quot; (also thinking about their name&quot; so it would not come off as too inappropriate, religiously speaking. Currently the idea is for them being ghosts of people who martyred themselves in the name of their Virtue, and that by canonizing them in some form they could grant Benedictions outside of the regular access of the conspiracy, but at a price to pay (following some kind of taboo/forcing upon you an obligation to your Virtue/something along those lines).<br /> <br /> The ides of entities who are tied to God's Wrath sound a lot more appropriate to the Long Night, who are much more fundamentalist in view as they seek signs for the End of Times, with all of its violent glory<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T14:07:49-08:00","id":1525326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1525223-nemeses-and-adversaries-organizational-horrors-brainstorming?p=1525319#post1525319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to ask about your stance on Inferno Demons. Compacts and Conspiracies that specialize in them (Malleus Maleficarum, The Lucifuge, The Long Night) do so through Christian lens. If we assume that these demons work as described in the Inferno supplement - creating their own backstories out of whole cloth, could they create one that is so &quot;out there&quot; that established exorcists would be at loss? With contemporary proliferation of popular fiction, an Acathartoi could swipe their backstory from a cartoon, Lovecraft fanfic, or a collectible card game wiki. Is that idea usable to you?</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal view would be yes, they are those evil lairs that create Testaments meant to glorify their names and heirarchies. The Lucifuge probably have a better understanding of it, which is why their section will deal with it in such a manner, but the Furies would be more vague in terms of origin (I'm actually conceptually moving them to Fiends, with the whole punishment and suffering thing they have going on for them).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I think Loyalists of Thule should get Nazis. Not Zombie Nazis, or wizard Nazis. Just Nazis. </div> </div> </div>Perfectly appropriate as antagonists, but I don't think you need special mechanics to run Nazis as antagonists :P maybe some fascist/racist/theosophical Mystery Cult could work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 11-11-2023, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T17:10:26-08:00","id":1525335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1525223-nemeses-and-adversaries-organizational-horrors-brainstorming?p=1525325#post1525325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't read The Outsider, but I did already had similar idea in relation to WandaVision. Some sort of a memory interloper that creates a &quot;community&quot; around it/shapes it to act in a certain manner. I assume that both ideas derive from the same themes, so I'll have to check it out.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's a good read. Anyway wandavision inspiration is good, though I warn you The Outsider lacks metaphysical effects on the world if that's what you're looking for with this sort of horror<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1525223-nemeses-and-adversaries-organizational-horrors-brainstorming?p=1525325#post1525325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tempters are indeed something I considered, alongside Maenads due to the whole Bacchanal thing they have going on. The other options also sound like an interesting concept to develop (potentially the Tempters could be connected to the ennui thing- they consume the Willpower you should have gotten from fulfilling your Vice, causing you to doing it more and more just top get the rush. Basically an analogy to drug addiction- it makes you feel good, but you need more of it as you become addicted)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds great. Would the abbey benefit from a horror that contrasts from their themes? I don't have any ideas but it's just question that may or may not be worth considering<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1525223-nemeses-and-adversaries-organizational-horrors-brainstorming?p=1525325#post1525325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting concept. Abyssal horrors of some kind is probably a must for them, in some shape or form.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, and i think the abyss is a good chance to open up on other goals since apparently they do R&amp;D<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1525223-nemeses-and-adversaries-organizational-horrors-brainstorming?p=1525325#post1525325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure that this book is exactly the place to deal with CofD's theological question of &quot;Where the F is Gaea?&quot;<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Let me switch that to communicate with something that MAY be connected to gaia...or be the void leviathans trapped in her body<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1525223-nemeses-and-adversaries-organizational-horrors-brainstorming?p=1525325#post1525325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahmm I'm still considering how to exactly write down the &quot;Saints&quot; (also thinking about their name&quot; so it would not come off as too inappropriate, religiously speaking. Currently the idea is for them being ghosts of people who martyred themselves in the name of their Virtue, and that by canonizing them in some form they could grant Benedictions outside of the regular access of the conspiracy, but at a price to pay (following some kind of taboo/forcing upon you an obligation to your Virtue/something along those lines).<br /> <br /> The ides of entities who are tied to God's Wrath sound a lot more appropriate to the Long Night, who are much more fundamentalist in view as they seek signs for the End of Times, with all of its violent glory<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>youre right about the Long Night, hadn't thought about that<br /> <br /> One more suggestion: the cainite heresy could have their Abels. Special revenants (spawned from cainites or maybe by humans who were collateral damage to cainites or a secret third thing) who's blood holds special qualities for the Rites of Denial. I just don't know how to further differentiate them from other revenants. Maybe make them a special imorata instead?<br /> <br /> I'll have more suggestions later","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-11T15:22:07-08:00","id":1525362,"title":"","content":"So let's go through the list of Core Compacts:<br /> <br /> <b>Ashwood Abbey:</b> as it was mentioned a few times, the Abbey should have something demonic in them, due to the whole Vice and Hellfire things they have going for them. That already gives us the <b>Tempters</b>, which were already mentioned. Those are basically Willpower sapping entities, creating Addiction Conditions related ton the Vice of the target, yet while they give some sort of benefit they both steal Willpower from Vice fulfillment and limit the gain from Virtue fulfillment (possibly replacing them in a manner similar to what happens to Soulless people). The second Horror which is very asked for is the <b>Maenads</b>, entities which inspire bacchanals, causing people to be driven mad with passion around them as they are lost to their urges- with them drawing Abbey hunters who either seek the rush or with them crushing the Abbey parties, turning everything into full blown chaos and making them into a constant &quot;nuisance&quot; to their fun. The last idea is that of <b>Lures</b>- those are people who draw monsters towards them, due to having a higher amount of supernatural within their form (similar to Sleigh Beggy from the Ancient Magus Bride), and as such they are often being used by the compact as the &quot;center of the party&quot;- whether they like it or not.<br /> <br /> <b>Long Night:</b> the Christian fundamentalists who fight as messengers of God are another conspiracy with religious themes, and as such likely to deal with proper Horrors. The first would be the <b>Grigori</b>- standard Fallen Angels (or at least self proclaimed ones) that were caged by God. Let's go in an angle similar to the Earthbound from Fallen- those are grand idols which demand blood sacrifice and are able to possess those who come in touch with them or swear fealty to the bound demon lord. Going with the theme of using Fallen's apocalyptic world, we can go with the <b>Messengers</b> as angelic beings that endow hunters with the power to fight the darkness, yet their zeal drives them mad, turning them into &quot;heavenly slashers&quot; of some sort. Finally, let's have the whole &quot;charisma&quot; thing that evangelical sects usually have and flip it on its head- the <b>Preachers</b> are individuals with a unique Devil Tongue that can convince others that they have performed miracles, healed the sick and banished possessions, yet this is all just falsehoods- allowing them to establish dark cults of personality as their followers are dying in their name.<br /> <br /> <b>Loyalists of Thule:</b> well let's get the low hanging fruit out of the way and just put the <b>Rmoahals</b> as a Horror in a similar manner as I already presented them in my Dark Eras book- vestigial remnants of pre-human species lurking within people's DNA, waiting to be triggered into a horrifying and sorcerous majesty of the long gone Giants. In terms of a more human kind of antagonists (which are indeed appropriate for this compact), such as some Mystery Cult in the style of the <b>Lemurians</b> which is both explicitly racist and attempts at finding the &quot;lost civilization of the Aryans&quot; and &quot;purify humanity&quot;. Another thing which would be appropriate for them is some sort of a God Machine related threat, considering that the compact (or more exactly its predecessors) are featured in Into the Cold- it could be the <b>Thule Infrastructure</b>, a sentient Infrastructure that corrupts the minds of those under its effect to adapt the Angelic Missions that lead towards re-creating Thule, yet at the cost of creating glitches in reality. Finally, something related to ghosts also seems to be needed to the compact- the <b>Librarians</b> are a special form of Eaters of the Dead that devour the memories of the ghosts that they eat, preserving them in their flesh. This means that they are both treasure troves of knowledge- at least, they would have been if they were obsessed with hiding it from the &quot;unworthy&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>Network 0:</b> the Truth Seekers are those hunters who have to constantly fight to reveal the truth. As such, the first enemy that they are probably going to have to deal with is the <b>Antimemetic</b>- similar concept to what seen in SCP, this horror seems to not merely defy perception and documentation, but also drains memories and obscure its surroundings- videos get corrupted, photos distorted, sound recording filled with white noise as they whisper and speak. By doing so, not only that the compact have trouble at documenting it, it also wrecks their own existing documents. Then we would have a more memetic horror- the <b>Fun Time Meme</b>. Suggested by Flyboy in the Discord, this Horror is partially based around the Smiley Face Killer Theory and serves as an information hazard- those who get exposed to the meme risk at getting brainwashed, becoming murderers who always kill in the same manner and leave the writing &quot;Fun Time&quot; on a nearby wall, only to completely forget that they have performed the act. Finally, let's go a bit Pain Prophet here and let's have the <b>Silence</b>- a strange phenomenon that takes the form of radio waves of an unknown source, where when received and translated creates a occult symbol that allows an eldritch horror to partially manifest in reality, devouring information in its solar corona. <br /> <br /> <b>Nine Stars:</b> The most basic Horror for those guys should be based around a form of slashers- the <b>Four Perils</b> refer to four artifacts where each contains a demonic desire to murder that transforms those under their influence into a special form of a supernatural murderer, devoted to bring ruin to wherever they go. On the other hand, we can go with the Eater of Names that seems to cause the slasher epidemic in the first place and have the <b>Name Eaten</b> as a Horror they have to deal with- those individuals have lost their True Names to the ancient Firstborn, and gain the ability to steal the names of those they murder in order to take their place in the world, yet as they avoid killing the hunger consumes them from within, forcing them to feast on more and more names to silence the everlasting call. <br /> <br /> <b>Null Mysteriis:</b> the scientific oriented compact basically seeks to understand the truth about the supernatural, which means that they are likely to deal with similarly scientific horrors. The <b>Eveans</b> are a special breed of Horrors that defy the ability of the compact to easily categorize it- known as the &quot;Children of Eve&quot; among the more mystical groups, those Horrors have the strange ability to adapt and evolve to circumstances, allowing them to constantly change their features and capabilities depending on the danger in which they are found (think the Hard to Kill reptile from SCP, just a little bit less OP). While the Eveans serve as the biological angle of the compact, the <b>Resonance</b> serves as the physical one- those are basically ephemeral manifestations of the fundamental force of the universe- time, space, gravity, entropy and so forth. In a way, they serve as the &quot;angels of the universal constants&quot;, serving as both manipulators of reality and present cosmological question to the compact as they try to comprehend the idea that gravity as its own divine messengers.<br /> <br /> <b>SWORN:</b> the protectors of the indigenous people who seek to rebuild their past from the remnants of colonialism, they have to deal with both entities which represent invasive species and the horrors which now lurk without stories to protect from them. Let's start from the <b>Water Serpents</b>- great cryptids who reside in lakes that each holds their own set of behavior and codes which allow it to drown those who do not follow the rules that only they now remember. As the reconstruction of stories and mythic monsters fits a lot of Beast's themes, let's have the <b>Boogeymen</b>: an astral horror that is literally weaved from stories and urban legends, and will never be destroyed permanently as long as the story is being told yet the story also details the only way it can be put down (temporarily). As for the last horror, let's have something a bit more abusive- the <b>Blue Rose</b> is a special plant from the Hedge that both has supernatural capabilities and serves as a gate for the Fae to reach beyond the Thorns by basically terraforming the local environment into a Arcadian realm, allowing strange monstrosities to form and disrupt the local ecology.<br /> <br /> <b>Union:</b> as it was already discussed, the <b>Gardeners</b> serves as the first Horror for this compact- those monsters are memory interlopers, not merely establishing themselves within the minds of those they prey upon but also create a strange, hivemind like community, conditioning them to behave in the manner they perceive as &quot;polite&quot; or &quot;acceptable&quot;, who also generally have powerful mind altering and illusion weaving abilities to those under their command. The second horror was again suggested by Flyboy- a Lowerdepthian species that feasts upon social connections and empathy- let's call it the <b>Atropoi</b>. Those Thread Cutters cause those who are affected by them to lose meaning to the &quot;social contract&quot;, disrupting their attachments and causing them to be unable to functional parts of society. Allow a Atropos to roam free for too long, and society itself will fall into chaos. Finally, let's have the <b>Toil</b>- a strange condition that infects people through teamwork. Each Toil is a special form of mental infection, leading those under its effect to follow certain patterns and devote their lives to a process which holds no meaning- crafting perfectly even squares out of wood, digging circles in the ground or make pyramids out of skulls. Those who try to understand the meaning of the process or take part in helping with it risk at falling victim to the Toil, which only stops when all infected work themselves to death to produce a product without a buyer and which has no value. Those who try to disrupt their work, however, will anger those under the Toil's effect, who will not hesitate using violence to protect its &quot;process&quot;.<br /> <br /> This is it for the Core concepts. Feel free to provide feedback on those, and I'll add them also to the outline of the project before moving to the next group of orgs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-12T12:02:14-08:00","id":1525384,"title":"","content":"About the maenads. Perhaps have them be a spontaneous becoming? Like some sorta state mortals reach through sheer hedonism. In this way you can tap into this theme of the line between hunter and monster, and the inhuman excess of the Abbey in an internal way.<br /> <br /> Crossroad Convoy: going off a possible promethean connection, maybe a hitchhiking petrificati with a twist? Instead of being dead, it's a constant wasteland producing golem that constantly seeks out transportation. Transport it, and you're stuck with a being with a wasteland catching up with him until you drop it off. Or leave it there, and let the area get worse and become a tale of the road. They may also benefit from a devil at the crossroads type horror<br /> <br /> the Illuminated brotherhood: a special drug would be perfect. Otherwise perhaps connections to the Astral along with the Shadow. Maybe a special urging brought on by their constant exposure to hallucinogens or a special loci due to perceiving it so often? I feel like they'd benefit most from a horror that takes advantage of what's the Shadow and what's just the high in their heads.<br /> <br /> Edit: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> just curious, are these supposed to be the &quot;most relevant&quot; supernatural oddities among the conspiracies? I noticed in your AKD book there are plenty of horrors unique to them in some way, from prometheans to ananke manipulators, but aren't listed for the AKD in this new thread. Do you consider them somewhat different in role to the conspiracy? Just wondering since the psychopomp for VASCU and Lures for Abbey seem to be more ally/exploited resource than nemesis","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 11-15-2023, 01:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T13:51:35-08:00","id":1525479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1525223-nemeses-and-adversaries-organizational-horrors-brainstorming?p=1525384#post1525384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About the maenads. Perhaps have them be a spontaneous becoming? Like some sorta state mortals reach through sheer hedonism. In this way you can tap into this theme of the line between hunter and monster, and the inhuman excess of the Abbey in an internal way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I generally prefer the maenads as their own horror- but I'm pretty sure that the people who bear the Tempters and the Lures themselves also easily blur the line between the human and the inhuman by themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Crossroad Convoy: going off a possible promethean connection, maybe a hitchhiking petrificati with a twist? Instead of being dead, it's a constant wasteland producing golem that constantly seeks out transportation. Transport it, and you're stuck with a being with a wasteland catching up with him until you drop it off. Or leave it there, and let the area get worse and become a tale of the road. They may also benefit from a devil at the crossroads type horror </div> </div> </div>Some form of petrificati could work indeed, would still need to think how to make it into a unique being other than something found in some other book. Crossroad devils are always cool.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> just curious, are these supposed to be the &quot;most relevant&quot; supernatural oddities among the conspiracies? I noticed in your AKD book there are plenty of horrors unique to them in some way, from prometheans to ananke manipulators, but aren't listed for the AKD in this new thread. Do you consider them somewhat different in role to the conspiracy? Just wondering since the psychopomp for VASCU and Lures for Abbey seem to be more ally/exploited resource than nemesis </div> </div> </div>As you might have noticed, I have changed the name of the project in the google docs from &quot;Nemeses and Archenemies&quot; to &quot;the Fittest&quot;. This represents a change in attitude in this project- those entities are not meant to only be the &quot;worst enemies of the orgs&quot; but entities which have a special relations with the orgs, either adapting to them or vise versa- for example, being useful for a group means that they won't see them as enemies, but a Lure would definetly won't like to be abused by the Abbey, and a Psychopomp will not necessary want to endanger their lives by linking to a murderer. For your other question, an AKD only splat book it makes sense to have a plethora of different enemies, but for a book containing all of those orgs must have a smaller scope for each org, which would mean we would have to choose the ones most appropriate. As the AKD favors hunting shifters and witches, those two horrors are a natural fit for the org, and the Daktyloi and Relic Eaters both pose a threat directly to the AKD. The Agathodaimon are a product of Labyrinths, again being very appropriate to the org. So yeah, those horrors, imo, are the most appropriate ones when considering the AKD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T14:16:30-08:00","id":1525482,"title":"","content":"Sorry I didn't notice the change. Anyway yeah I get your preference with the Abbey, I know the lures def already had that spot, I just didn't know if you'd find worth in the idea that Abbey who party hard enough become chosen maenads.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the petrificati thing is rough idea, it def needs more fleshing out<br /> <br /> Thank you on the explanation for the antagonists and such, i was a bit confused. And yeah I figured that would be the answer to AKD number in the book. It only makes sense a conspiracy specific book has more.<br /> <br /> Also, do you still plan on updating the compact end game theories?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T15:03:27-08:00","id":1525484,"title":"","content":"Conspiracy Theories for Compacts is on the plan, but in lower priority- I work when inspiration hits, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T15:16:04-08:00","id":1525486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1525223-nemeses-and-adversaries-organizational-horrors-brainstorming?p=1525484#post1525484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conspiracy Theories for Compacts is on the plan, but in lower priority- I work when inspiration hits, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha! Sorry if it sounded like I was trying to rush, I wasn't lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-20T18:28:52-08:00","id":1525705,"title":"","content":"Just in case you wanted me to post it here instead<br /> <br /> Bear Lodge: much like the AKD have their werebulls, would the Lodge benefit from the Cernunni you made? It seems like a good fit.<br /> <br /> Illuminated brotherhood: thinking on it more, what about sometimes, they make a spirit born directly from their hallucinations from drugs? The result is a strange and fluid spirit familiar. And think of it as having a &quot;chasing the dragon&quot; effect on the hunter<br /> <br /> Les Mysteres: I think them having some unique interaction with accidentally having Wounded spirits would be good to have, but I'm really struggling on what twist we can do with werewolves. Maybe spirit possessed ones? And what about shadow occultism?<br /> <br /> EDIT: perhapsperhaps Endowment related issue where something bad happens from Rites Du Chuval having Wounded spirits Ride the Les Mysteres<br /> <br /> Knights of Saint George: The Waking dreams-pockets of reality that are &quot;proof&quot; of the Knights failing their mission, when reality begins to break as the faceless angels grow restless in their sleep<br /> <br /> Finally the Cainite Heresy: moving on from the Adam&quot; revenants, what about a vampire covenant/shadow cult/what have you called something like The Denied-vampires focused on gaining back what blood Sorcery was lost all the way back in Rome","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 12-24-2023, 12:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-20T04:33:48-07:00","id":1538939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1525223-nemeses-and-adversaries-organizational-horrors-brainstorming?p=1525284#post1525284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Division 6: Rebel Agents. Those agents who have Awakened, but whose training with the division has made a new kind of Banisher that is unable to get rid of their shard of the abyss. The result is a &quot;rebel&quot; who has it out for the Division while still able to completely suppress magic. For some strange reason may be wanted alive by Mr. Jones. Another option could be some special type of abyssal verge that represent what happens when reality doesn't just reach its breaking point but is utterly shattered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've thought about something like this, but not so much as <i>enemies</i>. More like a desirable end-state for Division 6 hunters. Here's my new Compact Status merit.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Communal Sleeper merit<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Strained merit. You can risk Willpower on Paradox rolls you cause or Dissonance rolls you make.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Fitful Slumber merit. For each supernal or abyssal phenomenon you witness, choose whether you are a Sleeper or a Sleepwalker. This choice also applies to (your Presence+Empathy) of your Sleeper allies. As a Sleeper, you face a breaking point (deferred by the Strained merit as usual) and cause Paradox. As a Sleepwalker, you do not necessarily face a breaking point and you do not cause Paradox. You never suffer Quiescence, and you can choose to exclude any abyssal or supernal phenomenon from the effects of your Dissonance. You can spend a Willpower point to have your Dissonance affect an abyssal entity as though it were supernal.<br /> From this point on, you can gain supernatural merits without losing the ability to choose to be a Sleeper. You could conceivably even Awaken (as a Harrowed Banisher) without losing the ability to Sleep or being disqualified from taking merits that require you not to be supernatural. If you do, your Fitful Slumber bonus offsets penalties from being Harrowed .<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, and you should really take the Support Network merit from Hurt Locker, but Division 6 doesn't provide it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28549,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","user":"Sikander","date":". 07-20-2024, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-20T14:42:58-07:00","id":1538952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1525223-nemeses-and-adversaries-organizational-horrors-brainstorming?p=1538939#post1538939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've thought about something like this, but not so much as <i>enemies</i>. More like a desirable end-state for Division 6 hunters. Here's my new Compact Status merit.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Communal Sleeper merit<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Strained merit. You can risk Willpower on Paradox rolls you cause or Dissonance rolls you make.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Fitful Slumber merit. For each supernal or abyssal phenomenon you witness, choose whether you are a Sleeper or a Sleepwalker. This choice also applies to (your Presence+Empathy) of your Sleeper allies. As a Sleeper, you face a breaking point (deferred by the Strained merit as usual) and cause Paradox. As a Sleepwalker, you do not necessarily face a breaking point and you do not cause Paradox. You never suffer Quiescence, and you can choose to exclude any abyssal or supernal phenomenon from the effects of your Dissonance. You can spend a Willpower point to have your Dissonance affect an abyssal entity as though it were supernal.<br /> From this point on, you can gain supernatural merits without losing the ability to choose to be a Sleeper. You could conceivably even Awaken (as a Harrowed Banisher) without losing the ability to Sleep or being disqualified from taking merits that require you not to be supernatural. If you do, your Fitful Slumber bonus offsets penalties from being Harrowed .<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, and you should really take the Support Network merit from Hurt Locker, but Division 6 doesn't provide it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That last one isn't a hunter anymore. That's a mage. Something the Division does NOT want. They want to stop reality manipulation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-20T14:59:14-07:00","id":1538953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1525223-nemeses-and-adversaries-organizational-horrors-brainstorming?p=1538952#post1538952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That last one isn't a hunter anymore. That's a mage. Something the Division does NOT want. They want to stop reality manipulation</div> </div> </div> </div>An actual Harrowed Awakening would be a chronicle-defining event. If it looks like I'm offering it as a bennie for Status 5, I'm sorry. I'm just saying what would happen if the hunter <i>did </i>Awaken after achieving Status 5.<br /> <br /> <i>Division 6</i> wants to stop reality manipulation. <i>Mr. Jones</i> wants to achieve and maintain a monopoly on reality manipulation. A few more mages trained up since they were Sleepers in his special school? Gravy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28549,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","user":"Sikander","date":". 07-20-2024, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}